cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A four-arm benchmark of agentic bioinformatics platforms:
  smarts.bio, Biomni, Galaxy and an untooled control
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, its task set or its results, please
  cite it. Cite the commit hash or the Zenodo DOI so it is clear
  which version you read.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Orpaz
    given-names: Nir
    affiliation: smarts.bio
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7037-040X
repository-code: https://github.com/smartsbio/bio-agent-platform-benchmark
abstract: >-
  The same model answering the same prompts through one platform's
  tool server at a time, or through none at all. Four conditions,
  46 tasks each after audit, scored by a rubric judge blinded to
  condition. Built by smarts.bio, which is one of the conditions
  under comparison; the task set, the full run record and the raw
  transcript of every run are released so the result can be checked
  rather than taken on trust.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - genomics
  - variant calling
  - RNA-seq
  - BLAST
  - protein design
  - benchmark
  - LLM evaluation
  - large language models
  - LLM
  - AI agents
  - agentic AI
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - tool use
  - tool calling
  - Claude
  - reproducibility
  - smarts.bio
  - Biomni
  - Galaxy
